# module Shared HTTP turn lifecycle

Owns the single claim-adjacent request lifecycle used by Chat and Responses:
deadline, disconnect observation, pending-turn abort adoption, failure dispatch,
timer cleanup and guarded release.

# invariant Release always runs

The handler-specific release callback runs from `finally` on success, failure,
streaming return and tool handover. Timeout and disconnect remain separate flags.

Disconnect detection listens to `ServerResponse.close` before `writableEnded`, plus
`IncomingMessage.aborted` for an interrupted upload. Do not use
`IncomingMessage.close`: on supported Node versions it also fires after an ordinary
fully-read request and is not proof that the response peer disappeared.
